Name: Protocol Buffers
Short Name: protobuf
URL: https://github.com/google/protobuf
License: BSD-3-Clause
License File: LICENSE
Version: 36.0
CPEPrefix: cpe:/a:google:protobuf:36.0
Revision: 3f17acbf7ffbda81db8be17505554c726e558bb2
Update Mechanism: Manual
Security Critical: yes
Shipped: yes

Steps used to create the current version (or roll a newer one):

0. Nuke third_party/protobuf from orbit (rm -rf `third_party/protobuf`). Note
   that this removes this README.chromium so you may want it open in code search
   or remember the steps up until 2. where you get it back.

1. Pull the release from https://github.com/google/protobuf/releases (Source
   code .tar.gz). Extract to `third_party/protobuf` (without version suffix),
   i.e. you may `$ mv protobuf-21.12 third_party/protobuf` or similar.

2. Add back chromium's on-upstream files (from this directory):

   $ git checkout origin/main -- BUILD.gn DEPS DIR_METADATA OWNERS \
     PRESUBMIT.py PRESUBMIT_test.py README.chromium \
     check_file_lists.py check_file_lists_test.py \
     compile_size_probe.py compile_size_probe_test.py \
     gen_extra_chromium_files.py proto_library.gni proto_sources.gni \
     proto_wkt.gni roll_protobuf.py roll_protobuf_test.py \
     ':(glob)patches/*'

   Note: The `patches/` directory is already a part of the protobuf repository,
   but it uses subdirectories (`patches/protobuf_vNN/`) for its content, while
   in Chromium we store our patches directly in `patches/`. Use a single
   `':(glob)patches/*'` pathspec so `*` stops at `/` instead of matching
   upstream's subdirectories (plain `'patches/*.patch'` still matches across
   `/`), and avoid separate `.patch` and `.md` globs (`git checkout` exits 1
   and restores nothing if any single pathspec matches no files).

   Note: Ideally we wouldn't do this but instead have a
   `third_party/protobuf/src/` subdirectory where upstream code goes directly
   into. That will require updating things outside this repository (at least
   `third_party/webrtc`) to agree on where the source code lives. I wouldn't be
   surprised if that also required Google-internal uses of protobuf from webrtc
   to also agree on `third_party/protobuf/src` so maybe this'll never happen?
   Here be dragons. Probably.

   Remove `compatibility/` (which contains large files that trip presubmit)
   before making a local `git commit` here:

   $ rm -rf compatibility

3. Apply patches in patches/ (see the description below):

   $ for patch in patches/*.patch; do patch -s -p1 < $patch; done

   When a patch fails, it's probably best to check out previous state (from 2)
   for any changes not inside the patches/ folder, fix the patch and then try to
   reapply everything. It's not a good idea to fix the error, forget to generate
   a patch and leave patches/ in a bad state.

   If a patch no longer applies it may not be needed, if so remove it and its
   description in this README.chromium file. Similarly try to eventually
   upstream any patches out of band from unblocking the roll so we can
   eventually remove it here as well.

   Probably worth committing locally here too.

4. Run "gen_extra_chromium_files.py" in the same directory as this file.

   $ ./gen_extra_chromium_files.py -C ../../out/Default

   This script builds Chromium's `protoc` and uses it to:
   - Remove `compatibility/` and pre-generated Well-Known Type `.pb.{cc,h}`
     files (`any`, `api`, `duration`, `empty`, `field_mask`, `source_context`,
     `struct`, `timestamp`, `type`, `wrappers`).
   - Regenerate bootstrapped C++ headers/sources (`descriptor.pb.{h,cc}` and
     `compiler/plugin.pb.{h,cc}`) with Chromium's compiler patches applied.
   - Generate `python/google/protobuf/descriptor_pb2.py` and
     `python/google/protobuf/compiler/plugin_pb2.py`.
   - Generate `python/google/protobuf/internal/python_edition_defaults.py`
     directly via `protoc --edition_defaults_out` (no Bazel required).

   Add and commit the generated files. Because `*_pb2.py` is in the `.gitignore`
   file for this directory, you need to add those files with `-f`:

   $ git add src/google/protobuf/descriptor.pb.{h,cc} \
     src/google/protobuf/compiler/plugin.pb.{h,cc} \
     python/google/protobuf/internal/python_edition_defaults.py
   $ git add -f python/google/protobuf/descriptor_pb2.py \
     python/google/protobuf/compiler/plugin_pb2.py

5. Update Version, CPEPrefix and Revision in this file.

   The revision should be set to the SHA1 of the commit that the release tag
   points to at the time of the roll.

6. Address breakages.

   The CQ will help you identify problems that need fixing.

   Manually update BUILD.gn and proto_sources.gni as necessary. Hopefully this
   means just adding or moving around some source files, but might also include
   tweaks like modifying compiler flags or macro defines. To see which source
   files upstream added or removed in `src/file_lists.cmake` since `origin/main`
   that `BUILD.gn` and `proto_sources.gni` do not follow yet, run:

   $ ./check_file_lists.py --old-rev origin/main

   You may need to add new code modifications and diffs in patches/ as well.
   To do this, make the necessary changes in your current local branch, and then
   run the following command to create a patch file with the correct paths:

   $ git diff --relative=third_party/protobuf > patches/your.patch

   In the case of multiple unrelated changes which should have their own
   indivudal patches, you can also add `-- path/to/file` to your `git` command.

   Remember to also update the patch description below.


Notes (hints) for the next roll(er):

* Run `third_party/protobuf/roll_protobuf.py check` before starting a roll (to
  verify no prior commit modified `src/` or `python/` without updating
  `patches/`) and again after completing the roll (to verify `patches/*.patch`
  reproduces the updated tree).
* Run
  `third_party/protobuf/compile_size_probe.py -C out/Default --save pre_roll`
  before starting a roll and
  `third_party/protobuf/compile_size_probe.py -C out/Default --compare pre_roll`
  after completing the roll to inspect header-size deltas, `#include` chains,
  and per-symbol codegen deltas (`--diff-ir` / `--diff-source`) before sending
  the CL to the `compile-size` trybot.
* Update README.chromium as you go so you don't forget (after step 2. above, so
  you don't nuke those changes).
* Any argument changes to `protoc_wrapper` in `third_party/protobuf/BUILD.gn`
  may require updating `build/config/siso/protoc_wrapper.star` as well.
* The protobuf wheel for vpython3 needs to stay in sync with this protobuf, at
  least if there are breaking changes in protobuf's python bindings. See
  https://chromium.googlesource.com/infra/infra/+/refs/heads/main/infra/tools/dockerbuild/README.wheels.md

Note about vpython:

Some Python scripts end up mixing protoc output from this copy of protobuf with
the google.protobuf module from vpython's protobuf. If Python scripts break due
to the vpython copy of protobuf, you may need to update the version in
//vpython.toml. See https://crbug.com/1320047.

Description of the patches:

- 0004-fix-shared-library-exports.patch

  This patch allows exporting protobuf symbols in Linux .so libraries, so
  that protobuf can be built as a component (see http://crrev.com/179806).
  Obsoleted upstream by `PROTOBUF_EXPORT` and `PROTOC_EXPORT` in `port_def.inc`,
  which already emit `__attribute__((visibility("default")))` when
  `PROTOBUF_USE_DLLS` and `LIBPROTOBUF_EXPORTS` / `LIBPROTOC_EXPORTS` are
  defined:
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/3f17acbf7ffbda81db8be17505554c726e558bb2/src/google/protobuf/port_def.inc#L332-L366.

- 0008-uninline_get_empty_string.patch

  Uninlines `GetEmptyStringAlreadyInited()` (`PROTOBUF_NOINLINE`) to reduce
  binary size across generated protobuf code. Upstreaming is tracked in
  https://crbug.com/567566717.

- 0010-uninline-generated-code.patch

  Uninlines generated `Swap()` methods (`PROTOBUF_NOINLINE`) to reduce binary
  size. Obsoleted upstream because generated move-assignment now calls
  `InternalSwap(&from)` directly rather than `Swap(&from)`:
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/3f17acbf7ffbda81db8be17505554c726e558bb2/src/google/protobuf/compiler/cpp/message.cc#L2173-L2181.

- 0022-Allow-deprecated-fields.patch

  Allows deprecated fields to be used without extra C++ compiler warnings.
  Upstreaming a variant is tracked in https://crbug.com/567566374.

- 0029-make-initializers-optimizable.patch

  Removes a static initializer from Linux and Android builds.

  Makes the InitProtobufDefaults() static initializer optimizable by Clang when
  built with libc++. It patches out the OnShutdownDestroyString call, which we
  do not need, and removes the thread-safe initialization. Thread safety is only
  needed if a static initializer spawns a thread which then calls
  InitProtobufDefaults() without synchronizing with the start of main().
  (Anything which happens after main() starts can rely on the initializer
  running.)

  Later updated to patch out PROTOBUF_DESCRIPTOR_WEAK_MESSAGES_ALLOWED code
  which was not optimizable. Upstreaming a variant is tracked in
  https://crbug.com/567566400.

- 0031-workaround-cfi-unrelated-cast.patch

  A workaround for Clang's Control Flow Integrity check for casting pointers to
  memory that is not yet initialized to be of that type for empty arrays, does
  not work, and still fails. This patch removes the workaround and instead
  disables cfi-unrelated-cast for the affected methods and simplifies them.

  See https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/issues/10186.
  See https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1294200#c26.
  Options for simplifying or upstreaming this patch are tracked in
  https://crbug.com/567655098.

- 0039-generate-mediapipe-anylite.patch

  Workaround to allow generating protobuf code compatible with
  third_party/mediapipe. This replaces checked-in precompiled .pb.cc files. See
  https://crbug.com/332939935 and https://crbug.com/567654677 for options to
  eliminate or simplify this patch.

- 0042-fix-undefined-protobuf-custom-vtable.patch

  Fixes the build when PROTOBUF_CUSTOM_VTABLE is not defined. Obsoleted upstream
  by
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/25e2bb7ca37cc35099a79921221b8196ed625849.

- 0044-trim-protoc-main.patch

  Remove parts of protoc's main.cc that aren't necessary for Chromium (languages
  such as C#, PHP, Ruby, etc.).

  The plan is to keep this patch as-is because trimming unused language
  generators from `protoc` is specific to Chromium's build and avoids compiling
  71 additional generator `.cc` files. See `patches/0044-trim-protoc-main.md`
  for details.

- 0045-string-resize.patch

  Replaces usage of absl internal string routines with std::string::resize().
  Upstreaming a variant is tracked in https://crbug.com/567567472.

- 0051-export-template-define.patch

  Adds some missing export defines to fix Windows component build. Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/68259eecb51b3523acea8338d322b1d43df0123b.

- 0052-remove-dynamic-annotations.patch

  This removes dynamic annotations (for containers; an ASAN tool). The use of
  absl's dynamic_annotations is banned in Chromium (see
  //third_party/abseil-cpp/BUILD.gn), on top of which, Protobuf's usage is
  buggy. PlacementNew copies RepeatedFields wholesale via memcp, which triggers
  false positive out-of-bounds reads. See
  https://github.com/google/sanitizers/wiki/AddressSanitizerContainerOverflow.
  Upstreaming is tracked in https://crbug.com/567566785.

- 0058-fix-messagelite-clear-declaration.patch

  Fixes an incomplete type compilation error for the member pointer parameter
  `clear` in the `ClassData` constructor when `MessageLite` is only forward
  declared. Obsoleted upstream by
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/25e2bb7ca37cc35099a79921221b8196ed625849.

- 0060-export-any.patch

  Add PROTOBUF_EXPORT macros to functions used by any.proto.

  The OSS version of protobuf bundles generated .pb.{cc,h} files for full
  versions of well-known types (including any.proto) and assumes they are
  built together with protobuf. Chrome does not use protobuf_full in
  production, and thus does not use the bundled WKTs, instead generating lite
  versions. These versions can reside in a different component, and that's why
  those symbols need to be exported. Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/4fa81d0204609137eefbba7b88cccec4c90ee228.

- 0061-fix-invalid-enum-class-export.patch

  Removes invalid PROTOBUF_EXPORTs on enum classes in text_format.h.
  Under C++ / MSVC, dllexport attributes cannot be applied to enum classes,
  which triggers -Wignored-attributes under Clang on Windows component builds.
  Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/05ce295e1381a448bbd11a6309c8de2d716f4f74.

- 0062-fix-dllexport-explicit-instantiation-decl.patch

  Fixes -Wdllexport-explicit-instantiation-decl compiler warning in map_field.h
  and map_field.cc by replacing the unconditional PROTOBUF_EXPORT with
  PROTOBUF_EXPORT_TEMPLATE_DECLARE (which resolves to empty) and
  PROTOBUF_EXPORT_TEMPLATE_DEFINE (which resolves to dllexport/dllimport) to
  correctly declare and export explicit template instantiations. Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/31d1cbab9f7312fd97d54d520cc599efa804b4ad.

- 0064-time-util-no-export.patch

  Do not export symbols in time_util.h.

  This util was meant to be compiled with protobuf full. Since Chromium uses
  protobuf lite (and lite WKTs, such as duration and timestamp), we can't make
  it a part of protobuf as we would get a dependency cycle. Not exporting
  symbols allows us to use it as a separate target.

  The plan is to keep this patch as-is because `time_util` is compiled outside
  the `protobuf_lite` component and would otherwise fail with
  `-Winconsistent-dllimport` on Windows component builds. See
  `patches/0064-time-util-no-export.md` for details.

- 0065-gzip-stream-no-export.patch

  Do not export symbols in gzip_stream.h.

  This util was meant to be compiled with protobuf full. However, it depends on
  zlib, so instead of making Chromium's protobuf depend on zlib, the utility is
  compiled as a separate target, and not exported.

  The plan is to keep this patch as-is because `io_gzip_stream` is compiled
  outside the `protobuf_lite` component and would otherwise fail with
  `-Winconsistent-dllimport` on Windows component builds. See
  `patches/0065-gzip-stream-no-export.md` for details.

- 0067-disable-early-nodiscard.patch

  Disables PROTOBUF_FUTURE_ADD_EARLY_NODISCARD in port_def.inc as well as
  [[nodiscard]] on generated message and enum methods in message.cc and enum.cc
  to prevent cascading [[nodiscard]] compilation errors across Chromium and
  third-party callers (e.g. MediaPipe). Options for simplifying or eliminating
  this patch are tracked in https://crbug.com/567654954.

- 0068-remove-arena-heavy-includes.patch

  Removes `absl/strings/str_format.h` and `absl/hash/hash.h` from `arena.h`
  and removes unused `AbslStringify`, `ArenaPtrContainerHash`, and
  `AbslHashValue` implementations on `Arena::UniquePtr` and `Arena::Ptr` to
  avoid massive compile size and build time bloat across every translation unit
  that includes `.pb.h`. Obsoleted in practice because `io/coded_stream.h`
  transitively includes `absl/strings/cord.h`, which already pulls
  `absl/strings/str_format.h` and `absl/hash/hash.h` into every `.pb.h`:
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/blob/3f17acbf7ffbda81db8be17505554c726e558bb2/src/google/protobuf/io/coded_stream.h#L113.

- 0069-remove-btree-map-includes.patch

  Removes `absl/container/btree_map.h` from `extension_set.h` and `map.h` by
  defining `LargeRepBase` in `extension_set.h` (with inline size tracking) and
  moving `LargeMap` into `extension_set.cc`. Keeps `ExtensionSet::Size()` inline
  and simplifies LargeMap iteration. Eliminates btree_map template overhead
  across all translation units that include `.pb.h`. Upstreaming is tracked in
  https://crbug.com/567608581.

- 0070-fix-deprecated-get-enum-in-message.patch

  Removes [[deprecated]] attribute from Reflection::GetEnum and
  Reflection::GetRepeatedEnum in message.h (deprecated upstream for removal in
  Q1 2027 in favor of GetEnumValue / GetRepeatedEnumValue) to avoid
  -Wdeprecated-declarations compilation errors across remaining third-party
  callers (fuzztest, tflite, ink). Options for simplifying or eliminating this
  patch are tracked in https://crbug.com/567655036.

- 0071-remove-log-include-from-descriptor-h.patch

  Removes `absl/log/log.h` include from `descriptor.h` to avoid macro clashes
  with Chromium's `base/logging.h` (LOG, PLOG, DLOG, VLOG, etc.). Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/9a59883bc21943f3bec2c7e2743294446193dd4d.

- 0072-remove-version-stamp.patch

  Scrubs out the non-OSS `kVersionStampBuildHasHardeningProtobuf` version
  stamp block from `port.cc`. Upstreamed in
  https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/commit/fa52ce297c1bd24af9c7785de2d29744edbca485.
